## Summary

I've successfully implemented **US-008 - Exportar Reportes de Auditoría** (Export Audit Reports). Here's what was delivered:

### Implementation Details

**Files Created:**
- `backend/src/utils/exportReports.js` - PDF and XLSX generation utilities

**Files Modified:**
- `backend/src/api/audit/routes/audit.js` - Added `GET /api/audit-logs/export` endpoint
- `backend/src/api/audit/services/audit.js` - Added `exportAuditLogs()` method with SHA-256 hashing
- `backend/src/api/audit/controllers/audit.js` - Added `export()` method with format handling
- `backend/package.json` - Added `pdfkit` and `xlsx` dependencies

### Features Implemented

✅ **PDF Export** - Formatted reports with headers, summaries, and embedded digital signature
✅ **XLSX Export** - Structured spreadsheets with Summary and Logs sheets
✅ **Digital Signatures** - SHA-256 hash for integrity verification (in X-Audit-Hash header and embedded in reports)
✅ **Complete Filtering** - By date range (startDate/endDate), user ID, entity type, and entity ID
✅ **Full Audit Trail** - All data included: action, entity details, user, timestamp, IP address, changes (oldValue/newValue)
✅ **Permission Control** - Requires `VIEW_AUDIT_LOGS` permission (same as regular audit log viewing)
✅ **Quality Checks** - Both `npm run lint` and `npm run typecheck` pass

### Example API Usage
```
GET /api/audit-logs/export?format=pdf&startDate=2026-07-01&endDate=2026-07-31&userId=5
GET /api/audit-logs/export?format=xlsx&entityType=project&userId=3
```

